{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1355836-what-would-you-change-if-demon-the-descent-got-a-new-edition","id":1355836,"title":"What would you change if Demon the Descent got a new edition?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-19T07:08:39-08:00","id":1355836,"title":"What would you change if Demon the Descent got a new edition?","content":"What would you change if Demon the Descent got a new edition?<br /> <br /> My list of quick changes:<ul><li>Make God-Machine Angels have their own creation rules separate from the Ephemeral Entity rules. Angels shouldn't manifest, instead they should have Covers and Angelic Forms.</li> <li>Lean more into Bio-Mechanical Horror more. Angels, Cryptids, and Gadgets being presented with a mix of organic and inorganic components.</li> <li>Expand the God-Machine as antagonist to other entities who are trying to collect Angels as their servants/slaves. Demons being the closest things Angels have to a free form.</li> <li>Establish a supernatural community of Demons. My only issue with Demon the Descent so far is that there isn't a sense of scaling with Demons. A high Primum Demon isn't easily identified, except for the glitches they have accrued. And even then Demons seem like they would rather live separate from one another than together. Maybe if Archdemons acted as beacons for other Demons to rally behind. It's not an elegant solution, but I feel like there has to be a better way to organize Demon communities without them all being so underground that other demons can't find them.</li> <li>Hell Infrastructure vs Heaven Infrastructure. Establish what Hell can actually look like. Places where Angels cannot enter, where Demons have access to the equivalent of Angel Incepts. So in order for the God-Machine to take it back he has to send Non-Angel agents to destroy Hell infrastructure.</li> <li>Add an additional Antagonist that isn't Angel or Demon. I heard Mummy adding Immortals as antagonists and thought that was a great idea. But Angel vs Demon is very iconic I don't know who you'd add against them.</li> <li>Anti-Demon weapons. In mythology Demons do have weaknesses to Holy relics, Holy chanting, and other religious items. So it would make sense that there is some Demon Bane items that can affect Demons.</li> </ul>While I like the God-Machine I do also like the idea of other entities trying to fight for control over Angels. Angels are a servant species from all accounts in the books. It would make sense that some may have been corrupted/taken by other powerful entities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T14:09:27-08:00","id":1355943,"title":"","content":"I would very much like a two-column spread in which the left-hand column relates a scene or a series of scenes, and the right-hand column gives the mechanics that generated the scene, including the rational of the ST and Player, the calculation of the dice pool and the analysis of the result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T19:49:34-08:00","id":1355988,"title":"","content":"well 2nd edition is being made so...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T03:49:12-08:00","id":1356033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1355836-what-would-you-change-if-demon-the-descent-got-a-new-edition?p=1355988#post1355988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">well 2nd edition is being made so...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It uses 95% of the Revised Storytelling System (colloquially known as 2nd edition) so don't expect a second edition of Demon until the system reaches its third edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T18:13:42-08:00","id":1356207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1355836-what-would-you-change-if-demon-the-descent-got-a-new-edition?p=1356033#post1356033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It uses 95% of the Revised Storytelling System (colloquially known as 2nd edition) so don't expect a second edition of Demon until the system reaches its third edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought they were making a new edition? like corebook<br /> <br /> welp, guess I was wrong, so I'll give it a go.<br /> <br /> 1. more stuff on the pentagram<br /> <br /> 2. occult mechanics and how to interact with them<br /> <br /> 3. have it broaden its focus. right now demon heavily leans toward being about dismantling the God-Machine, so saboteurs largely seem to be the only relevant agency in terms of what the game allows for.<br /> <br /> 4. stop making demons so mechanical (and angels for that matter). they are said to sometimes be all tech, all organic, and BIO-mechanical. much of 1st edition was way too focused on them being robotic.<br /> <br /> 5. finally, make them more demonic. I'm ok with all the spy terminology and such, and keep that, it's good. but add more aspects that highlight what makes them...well, demonic. how they may use Infrastructure, their alien morals, etc. I understand the line between demonic and angelic is blurry at best, I'm talking about the line between Demonic and being spies.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Crap my bad <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a>, you meant it would be quite a while before 2nd edition is even announced for Kickstarter, correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T20:34:39-08:00","id":1356227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1355836-what-would-you-change-if-demon-the-descent-got-a-new-edition?p=1355943#post1355943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would very much like a two-column spread in which the left-hand column relates a scene or a series of scenes, and the right-hand column gives the mechanics that generated the scene, including the rational of the ST and Player, the calculation of the dice pool and the analysis of the result.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not a Demon thing so much as a &quot;help me understand the ludonarrative interplay of a scene&quot; thing.<ul><li>A little more up-front establishment that the God-Machine is, well, The Establishment, with all that that actually means. The lede's a little buried at present vis-a-vis the fact that, at any scale south of the existential, &quot;the God-Machine maintains the status quo&quot; combines with &quot;the God-Machine is fallible&quot; to mean &quot;the God-Machine regularly supports bad people doing bad things.&quot; It's a techno-organic edifice playing the role of the Gnostic Devil, and its vested interest in the fulfillment of its projects and its dispassionate approach to same should not obfuscate the fact that it is doing what it does to benefit itself first and foremost. Thinking of it as just a machine that's malfunctioning here and there is committing the same error it makes in its approach to demonic individuality, and while that's fun to realize as a piece of subtext, it could probably be buried a little closer to the surface than it is.</li> <li>A little more mechanical rigor for glitches would go a long way, since the implication seems to be that they're the preferred way of venting compromises and logically one of the main giveaways to set an investigator on the trail to picking apart a Cover.</li> <li>In a context where we now have a more or less consistent baseline framework for conspiracies from Deviant (which it's been lamented would have been useful to have back when designing more involved takes on Infrastructure) and Mummy 1e put out rules for occult architecture towards the end of its run, the only thing I can really conceive of as not guaranteeing Tempters and Psychopomps more stuff to play with in a new edition is wordcount and pagespace.</li> <li>Front-loading the complexities of the angel-to-exile-to-demon continuum and all the various ways the Machine winds up arrayed against itself, I feel, can only heighten the Cold War atmosphere of not knowing who's doing what and why. Let the mechanical lines blur a little without repeating the confusion brought about by &quot;angels with Cover-equivalent Infrastructure don't actually interact with the Manifestation system, but their statblocks still bother to list Twilight Form et al.&quot;</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T06:14:41-08:00","id":1356283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1355836-what-would-you-change-if-demon-the-descent-got-a-new-edition?p=1356207#post1356207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Crap my bad <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>, you meant it would be quite a while before 2nd edition is even announced for Kickstarter, correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>I highly doubt OPP has started planning for a second edition of Demon. This edition of the system is still new, with most games still having few supplements, and four of them not even having had their core books released yet. In short, it should be years before a new edition of the system would be considered for development, and I don't think they'll do a second edition of Demon before that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T08:45:27-08:00","id":1356302,"title":"","content":"I think there can definitely be more of the marriage between technology and occult. It\u2019s not that the occult is actually technology so much as that occult and tech are compatible, if that makes sense. Demons don\u2019t have to be completely organic, some have cybernetics, others are completely inorganic statues made of demonic marble. Some can even be fully robotic. <br /> <br /> I\u2019d like to see demons confront a demonic seal; and one demon says \u201cClearly the pattern in the seal is a code that completely locks down any Demon who walks into it\u201d while another says \u201cThe seal is a representation of holy energy, meant to isolate any demonic energy that passes over it\u201d while another says \u201cThe ancient script that surrounds the seal is a 12th century prayer to trap demons, created by a holy man who banished demons from his village.\u201d And all of them are correct. <br /> <br /> You have one demon who can overwrite the code of the seal, another who can manipulate the power flow of the seal, and another who can speak a counter spell to unlock the seal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T10:02:27-08:00","id":1356315,"title":"","content":"My biggest wish is a revised mechanical handling of angels, and more explicit on page discussion of the mechanical asymmetries between demons and angels. The interplay between demons getting to do fuckall with Twilight and angels easily accessing twilight is barely discussed; this perturbs me. <br /> <br /> Demon talks a lot about tactics in the abstract and in the spy metaphor but falls down sometimes in explaining how those translate to details. The angels of its (awesome) fiction seem much more parallel to its demons than the mechanics we are actually given.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T17:49:28-08:00","id":1356404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DontEatRawHagis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1355836-what-would-you-change-if-demon-the-descent-got-a-new-edition?p=1356302#post1356302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019d like to see demons confront a demonic seal; and one demon says \u201cClearly the pattern in the seal is a code that completely locks down any Demon who walks into it\u201d while another says \u201cThe seal is a representation of holy energy, meant to isolate any demonic energy that passes over it\u201d while another says \u201cThe ancient script that surrounds the seal is a 12th century prayer to trap demons, created by a holy man who banished demons from his village.\u201d And all of them are correct.<br /> <br /> You have one demon who can overwrite the code of the seal, another who can manipulate the power flow of the seal, and another who can speak a counter spell to unlock the seal.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, here's the problem: these can all be correct, but they're all correct in the current edition as well and the reason the first one tends to get more press is because of what demons are.<br /> <br /> Demons use plain language for most of their terms for a number of reasons, least among them being that they have no native language of their own and the nature of their creator means wiretaps are everywhere, but the gist of it is this: demons aren't going to take kindly to being transparently mythologized to by their peers when they have a job to do.<br /> <br /> The God-Machine is a techgnostic take on the Demiurge, a Gnostic entity named by analogy to the role of craftsman, and the Unchained are tools of if not <i>pieces of </i>the God-Machine. Their technical language is plain because a) working behind the curtain means you don't need or have time for the theatrics of mythic language that Messengers mess with among mortals, and 2) an awful lot of them are demons because they're really upset at unclear communication or being outright lied to by their employer.<br /> <br /> Look at the things demons <i>do </i>use poetic terms for: themselves, their maker, their loyalist brethren, the fabled state of freedom many of them pursue, and the mysterious process that ostensibly guides them there. Things they're invested in that don't map plainly to descriptive language.<br /> <br /> They can use inflated prose to describe other stuff if they feel like romanticizing the processes, but selective pressure means romantic demons without a ruthless streak tend not to survive. The first demon is telling you what the thing does, the second demon is doing the same thing but with bells on, and the third one is doing the same thing but with the benefit of information the other two may not have been able to acquire themselves.<br /> <br /> What <i>does</i> fulfill the desire for more poetical demons, though\u2026<ul><li>A stronger integration of cults and stigmatics into the core game, much as other Second Editions have done with their mortal-adjacent secondary splats. Getting an outside view of how the Unchained operate (and how they tell you they're operating) should help tremendously with feeding the demand for more mythologized demons while still respecting the fact that they're rogue archons inclined to distrust simplified frameworks of good-versus-evil and it's-God-don't-worry-about-the-details. Mage and Mummy's newer emphasis on mortal support structures may likewise help somewhat with establishing demonic &quot;society.&quot;</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T19:30:19-08:00","id":1356417,"title":"","content":"Analysts in the core (really this is all in the core, I appreciate some of it has been in supplements but I don't like it when a game doesn't become good until supplements are out), more morally ambiguous (or flat out evil) things to do for advantages, probably crib something from Deviant or other Nemesis systems from games for mechanical support for angels and cults bent to hunt specific PCs down, keep the power level but fiddle with the all or nothing abilities so there's some leeway, some established Angel and Demons of fame or infamy so STs can have some big names to drop into games for plot hooks and wow factor. Also be more clear about the differences between occult matrices and infrastructure, and what infrastructure is (I don't think it got across very well) and capabilities of angels.<br /> <br /> It's a very good game as is, I don't think much really should be changed around, mostly just tightening up loose ends. The biggest and most common complaint I hear is just that it's not Demon the Fallen, but it never really tried to be so I don't think that's worth spending any concern over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T20:56:31-08:00","id":1356431,"title":"","content":"I've said elsewhere that I wish the rules for conspiracies in Deviant existed when I was writing the sections on Infrastructure for God-Machine Chronicle and Demon. Nodes/Linchpins --&gt; Conspiracies/Projects --&gt; Web of Pain so easily maps over to discrete Infrastructure/Linchpins --&gt; interconnected Infrastructure/Projects --&gt; God-Machine as entity, and it gives a mechanical way to approach and attack the God-Machine's interests (and to be hunted and attacked by its servants, in turn). So I'd love to rebuild Infrastructure systems with those newly learned lessons.<br /> <br /> I think it would also be good to clean up the depiction of what the God-Machine wants to do with/to its wayward servants. The idea that sometimes It wants to capture them, sometimes It wants to recycle them, and sometimes It just wants them eliminated isn't a problem in itself (counterintelligence often requires you to let known enemy agents continue to operate without check so that they don't realize that they're under tight surveillance, for example), but the fact that no explanation is given as to <i>why</i> It doesn't treat demons consistently is. There was a fair amount of exploring this question across various supplements, but I'd like to see them unified in a few paragraphs of the core.<br /> <br /> Finally, and this might be a bit more controversial, I'd like to de-emphasize Integrators as traitors looking for a chance to betray their fellow Unchained hard enough to earn redemption in the eyes of the God-Machine, which always struck me as more of an antagonist philosophy than a protagonist one. I like Integrators best as demons who want to &quot;fix&quot; the God-Machine, or who have taken up a task that is outside of their original mission (&quot;I'll return to It once I've raised my Cover's kids&quot;), or who have decided that the God-Machine isn't their <i>enemy</i>, just that they don't want to be servants anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T22:56:31-08:00","id":1356440,"title":"","content":"Modified form of the conspiracy rules a la Deviant for managing the consequences of compromises and modelling infrastructural projects.<br /> <br /> Support for trying to hack infrastructure to produce alternate output or even to hack together your own suborned infrastructure with ends towards output, which might well hook into the above. Flowers of Hell claimed to provide this but had very little mechanical support for doing much more than a few very specific tricks, regardless of the infrastructure.<br /> <br /> Straighten out clearly whether angels use material Cover like demons or ephemeral Manifestations, define how it works rather than leaving it to be inferred, remove the one they don't use.<br /> <br /> Simplify the pact system. It uses the structure of Changeling 1e's very versatile, customizable pledge system, but is not customizable enough to really benefit from it. The scaling Willpower cost is clumsy and fails to accomplish what it sets out to do. If you want to disincentivize demons from being too generous with their pact benefits, do it differently.<br /> <br /> Quibbliest wish: A cost for gadget projects more interesting than a Willpower dot, like needing to find and suborn particular types of infrastructure as workstations or supplies.<br /> <br /> Integrating the new conspiracy rules is the only real big overhaul. Demon doesn't need a huge update, a lot of it is fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T23:01:48-08:00","id":1356441,"title":"","content":"Oh! Big one that I'd like to not forget:<ul><li>Emphasize/Illustrate the particular oddity of the Machine that is arguably its strongest claim to divinity: the thing itself is so hidden as to be nonexistent. It dwells in all its work, but its work comprises everything from steam engines to times tables and its communication is always through intermediaries. It is an opportunistic parasite in the structure of structure, regardless of whether or not you believe it to be the same hypothetical entity that set the world in motion or that its stewardship is directly responsible for the continued existence of reality itself. The God-Machine has a reasonable claim on being divorced from the material reality it favors due to its connection to systems both concrete and abstract, and while its particular means of exerting influence are not so broad as to make up the whole of the universe, demons largely haven't taken leave of their senses when they speculate that some otherworldly phenomenon or another could possibly have its blueprints in the mix. The Demiurge is an Unmoved Mover sending its fragments scurrying through the tunnels of Order as it does its work, and the messiness of those tunnels and that work are part of why demonic Agendas break down the way they do \u2014 they call this thing God because it's impossibly vast, wields massive deific power, and seemingly cannot be wholly pinned down. Conspiracy can retreat under a grain of sand, and the space-saving abilities of angels are well-documented.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T12:29:33-08:00","id":1356514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1355836-what-would-you-change-if-demon-the-descent-got-a-new-edition?p=1356431#post1356431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've said elsewhere that I wish the rules for conspiracies in Deviant existed when I was writing the sections on Infrastructure for God-Machine Chronicle and Demon. Nodes/Linchpins --&gt; Conspiracies/Projects --&gt; Web of Pain so easily maps over to discrete Infrastructure/Linchpins --&gt; interconnected Infrastructure/Projects --&gt; God-Machine as entity, and it gives a mechanical way to approach and attack the God-Machine's interests (and to be hunted and attacked by its servants, in turn). So I'd love to rebuild Infrastructure systems with those newly learned lessons.<br /> <br /> I think it would also be good to clean up the depiction of what the God-Machine wants to do with/to its wayward servants. The idea that sometimes It wants to capture them, sometimes It wants to recycle them, and sometimes It just wants them eliminated isn't a problem in itself (counterintelligence often requires you to let known enemy agents continue to operate without check so that they don't realize that they're under tight surveillance, for example), but the fact that no explanation is given as to <i>why</i> It doesn't treat demons consistently is. There was a fair amount of exploring this question across various supplements, but I'd like to see them unified in a few paragraphs of the core.<br /> <br /> Finally, and this might be a bit more controversial, I'd like to de-emphasize Integrators as traitors looking for a chance to betray their fellow Unchained hard enough to earn redemption in the eyes of the God-Machine, which always struck me as more of an antagonist philosophy than a protagonist one. I like Integrators best as demons who want to &amp;quot;fix&amp;quot; the God-Machine, or who have taken up a task that is outside of their original mission (&amp;quot;I'll return to It once I've raised my Cover's kids&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, or who have decided that the God-Machine isn't their <i>enemy</i>, just that they don't want to be servants anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with the Integrators. they are actually my favorite Agenda and I feel the Corebook focuses WAY too much on the traitor ones (nothing wrong with those, I think those can even still BE played as PCs) and makes them sound ONLY like antagonists. the player and storyteller guide is definitely how I want them to be explored for a possible 2nd edition.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25291_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25291\" data-vbnamecard=\"25291\">DontEatRawHagis</a>, I'm sorry about being so rude. I thought the Brochure from way back said it was getting a new edition. again, sorry I was such a uninformed ass about it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T17:11:00-08:00","id":1356556,"title":"","content":"Speaking of the Idealists\u2026<ul><li>It would be great to see the category of &quot;exile&quot; actually engage with the lexicon's early allusion to being a liminal state reachable from both sides, if only because it offers a good midpoint or failstate for Integrator Hells in addition to helping blur the line between Unchained and loyalists.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-23T11:02:06-08:00","id":1356668,"title":"","content":"I'd really like it if the Pact mechanics:<ul><li>Ability to Demons store their rewards from Pacts as bargaining chips. For instance, give someone Striking Looks in exchange for their 4 Dots in Academics then use those 4 Dots of Academics in deals with College Students trying to pass exams. Essentially this is to avoid the &quot;Where does the money come from?&quot; problem that might happen. Demons could still make deals like those, but this would be a safer alternative.</li> <li>&quot;Where does the money come from?&quot; is a great premise and could result in Mortal Antagonists that become hunters or something worse. Imagine giving a person Striking Looks only for a model to become ugly overnight. She becomes obsessed with tracking down what did this to her. It's touched on in the Core books, but these people seem like they'd be the most common type of demon hunters.</li> <li>Supernatural Ability Pacts - Giving someone supernatural abilities like a Werewolf or Vampire, should create a more mundane version of those splats that doesn't conform to those groups.</li> <li>Suppression of Supernatural Ability - While the rule book says a demon can't steal a Vampire or Werewolf's powers as part of a soul pact, I really like the idea of trying to cure people of their affliction, but having disastrous consequences. For example, removing the Vampire part of a person doesn't delete it, Pacts are about equivalent exchange. Instead the Vampire part is splintered off as a physical embodiment of &quot;The Beast&quot;. So yes the Vampire becomes Mortal again, but now there is a homicidal Vampire that wants you back. Perhaps to keep this from causing too much damage Demons try to keep pacts like this limited to a short time frame.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T22:19:50-08:00","id":1362796,"title":"","content":"I would like to see a new edition updated to meet 2E conventions of layout and design. I'm just reading it through for the first time since its release, and it's painfully 1E.<br /> <br /> A full suite of Anchors and Touchstones (tied to Covers) would help underscore the alien mindset of the Unchained.<br /> <br /> The Cipher should be a means of not only achieving power, but a means of reaching Hell (if it exists), or a means of liberation. I'm reading this edition, and Hell and the Cipher seem to go nowhere. Like, the Cipher could be a backdoor into the God-Machine itself, or a means of hardening Cover against low-level compromises.<br /> <br /> I do like the idea of mortal demon-hunters and would-be Fausts interfering with operations. If the war between the G-M and the demons is the Cold War, then these conspiracies and covenants are the rogue states, with enough power to be useful, and enough knowledge to to leverage that utility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T23:31:52-08:00","id":1362804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1355836-what-would-you-change-if-demon-the-descent-got-a-new-edition?p=1362796#post1362796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to see a new edition updated to meet 2E conventions of layout and design. I'm just reading it through for the first time since its release, and it's painfully 1E.<br /> <br /> A full suite of Anchors and Touchstones (tied to Covers) would help underscore the alien mindset of the Unchained.<br /> <br /> The Cipher should be a means of not only achieving power, but a means of reaching Hell (if it exists), or a means of liberation. I'm reading this edition, and Hell and the Cipher seem to go nowhere. Like, the Cipher could be a backdoor into the God-Machine itself, or a means of hardening Cover against low-level compromises.<br /> <br /> I do like the idea of mortal demon-hunters and would-be Fausts interfering with operations. If the war between the G-M and the demons is the Cold War, then these conspiracies and covenants are the rogue states, with enough power to be useful, and enough knowledge to to leverage that utility.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You know Demon is already 2ed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T23:39:57-08:00","id":1362805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1355836-what-would-you-change-if-demon-the-descent-got-a-new-edition?p=1362796#post1362796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Cipher should be a means of not only achieving power, but a means of reaching Hell (if it exists), or a means of liberation.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is ostensibly what the Interlocks and final secret it provides are for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1355836-what-would-you-change-if-demon-the-descent-got-a-new-edition?p=1362804#post1362804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know Demon is already 2ed</div> </div> </div> </div>Demon is still in its First Edition, having been the first gameline made for the Revised Storytelling System. Any new edition of Demon would be a Second Edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T00:36:17-08:00","id":1362814,"title":"","content":"This may be the gadget lover in me, but I\u2019d prefer if it was explicitly a Sanctity Of Merits affair when dealing with ones that the player has created, much like with Tokens in Changeling. If Oneshots are carried over from 1e, it would be lovely if they were also made with something other than a willpower <i>dot</i> to make a limited number of one use items, which ties into the Sanctity Of Merits mention earlier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T02:38:10-08:00","id":1362826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1355836-what-would-you-change-if-demon-the-descent-got-a-new-edition?p=1362796#post1362796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A full suite of Anchors and Touchstones (tied to Covers) would help underscore the alien mindset of the Unchained.</div> </div> </div> </div>They already have Anchors in the form of Virtues and Vices that are supposed to be alien as to reinforce the alien mindset.<br /> Touchstones, while not a bad idea for longterm Covers, are not universally present in Revised Storytelling System (aka 2E) games, and their lack here does not imply that Demon isn't a Revised Storytelling System game (which it is, to like 90-95%).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1355836-what-would-you-change-if-demon-the-descent-got-a-new-edition?p=1362796#post1362796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Cipher should be a means of not only achieving power, but a means of reaching Hell (if it exists), or a means of liberation. I'm reading this edition, and Hell and the Cipher seem to go nowhere. Like, the Cipher could be a backdoor into the God-Machine itself, or a means of hardening Cover against low-level compromises.</div> </div> </div> </div>Supposedly the Cipher <i>is</i> the way to Hell, but it's woefully underdeveloped and completely dependent on the ST to come up with some explanation to what Hell means for your character. Mechanically speaking, though, unlocking your whole Cipher and getting closer to (if not reaching) Hell only grants you the final Interlock.<br /> In short, it is underwhelming, too dependent on non-informed character progression choices, and highly discouraging to homebrewing because any homebrew Embeds written up or found during the game will be guaranteed to not be the right Key because the Cipher was supposed to be planned out before any such Embeds were included. Hell, if you start a game before getting the Players' Guide you can be sure those Embeds won't be correct either.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1355836-what-would-you-change-if-demon-the-descent-got-a-new-edition?p=1362796#post1362796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to see a new edition updated to meet 2E conventions of layout and design. I'm just reading it through for the first time since its release, and it's painfully 1E.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1355836-what-would-you-change-if-demon-the-descent-got-a-new-edition?p=1362804#post1362804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know Demon is already 2ed</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1355836-what-would-you-change-if-demon-the-descent-got-a-new-edition?p=1362805#post1362805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demon is still in its First Edition, having been the first gameline made for the Revised Storytelling System. Any new edition of Demon would be a Second Edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Demon is in its first edition but using what is colloquially known as second edition rules (the Revised Storytelling System) but was released while OPP wasn't allowed to have an official second edition meaning Demon: The Descent is a first edition book (both being its own first edition and being released for the first edition of the system) written to be a second edition book (ruleswise) and is a bit of a horrible blend because of it. That's the reason for its horrible first edition layout and why it still references the World of Darkness rulebook despite being (mostly) a &quot;second edition&quot; game. I would say that it's to 90-95% a &quot;second edition&quot; game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-25T14:04:07-08:00","id":1363344,"title":"","content":"The Cipher is a journey without a destination, and I just want that character path rewarded. I'm not even mad at it, it's just that in a game about secrets and transcendence, just getting to &quot;you've maxed out your tech tree&quot; is a touch anticlimactic.<br /> <br /> What I want for 2e more than anything is texture. Vampire and Werewolf feel like sexy and savage benders to play through. Mage is obsessive, daunting, and expansive. That's the glow-up I'd love to see for Demon. There's such strong questions about Self among the Descent, the Cipher, and Covers, and that's what my suggestions about anchors, 'stones, and Embeds are lurching at.<br /> <br /> I guess if angels have virtues and vices, it's fair for demons to have them too, but I feel it ties them to humanity closer than I personally like. I see V&amp;Vs as a mark of an OEM soul, where jailbroken souls/substitutes are different enough that they just respond differently to adversity. Demons are outsiders, like Prometheans, which is why I feel it's more suitable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-25T14:26:19-08:00","id":1363349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1355836-what-would-you-change-if-demon-the-descent-got-a-new-edition?p=1363344#post1363344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess if angels have virtues and vices, it's fair for demons to have them too, but I feel it ties them to humanity closer than I personally like. I see V&amp;Vs as a mark of an OEM soul, where jailbroken souls/substitutes are different enough that they just respond differently to adversity. Demons are outsiders, like Prometheans, which is why I feel it's more suitable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're focusing so much on the name of those Anchors that you miss the fact that they have <i>different</i> Virtues and Vices. They work mechanically the same (which isn't far from how <i>any</i> such Anchors work) but the examples are very different, and they are so specifically to highlight how non-human angels and demons are from humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-25T14:44:40-08:00","id":1363350,"title":"","content":"I'm actually focusing on how Anchors have different mechanics, which are similar to Vs, but are still different. These differences exist to highlight aspects of a supernatural psychology now in place, and given how differently a fugitive interdimensional cyborg newly severed from a universal intelligence would probably come at the questions of willpower and identity, I wonder if sticking to the first draft is best \ud83d\ude09<br /> <br /> From the view you're espousing, why have ever bothered with cool shit like Blood &amp; Bone, or Mask &amp; Dirge? If they can be justified, why should Demon be denied? What's the benefit to sticking them with Virtues and Vices? They are probably the least human of any the splats, and the most dismissive of humanity.<br /> <br /> EDIT: They don't have &quot;different&quot; Virtues and Vices, either. The author suggests looking at these traits from the demonic mindset, and angel design rules suggest flipping them to drive home how inhuman they are, but this isn't essential to either creature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":969,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","user":"Verge","date":". 01-25-2020, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-25T15:50:00-08:00","id":1363359,"title":"","content":"Make some of the terminology easier to interpret. Had more than one occasion where I kept misunderstand how to design infrastructure. Also, more use of Angel Incepts. They keep leaving those out when they showcase new angel characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-26T12:59:38-08:00","id":1363497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1355836-what-would-you-change-if-demon-the-descent-got-a-new-edition?p=1363350#post1363350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the view you're espousing, why have ever bothered with cool shit like Blood &amp; Bone, or Mask &amp; Dirge?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, personally speaking, this is where I have always been. Promethean and Deviant are the only 2e gamelines that did anything interesting with alternate Anchors in my book, and Deviant did it by total renovation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-26T22:50:04-08:00","id":1363563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1355836-what-would-you-change-if-demon-the-descent-got-a-new-edition?p=1363344#post1363344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Cipher is a journey without a destination, and I just want that character path rewarded. I'm not even mad at it, it's just that in a game about secrets and transcendence, just getting to &quot;you've maxed out your tech tree&quot; is a touch anticlimactic.<br /> <br /> What I want for 2e more than anything is texture. Vampire and Werewolf feel like sexy and savage benders to play through. Mage is obsessive, daunting, and expansive. That's the glow-up I'd love to see for Demon. There's such strong questions about Self among the Descent, the Cipher, and Covers, and that's what my suggestions about anchors, 'stones, and Embeds are lurching at.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok - very personal opinion follows.<br /> <br /> I like the CoD products because they focus a bit more on storytelling than tactics (I'm looking at you DnD). You are rewarded for your character making dramatically interesting choices.<br /> <br /> <i>Some</i> of the CoD storylines, I have come to understand, focus on catharsis. In particular, Changeling (AFAIK) focuses on surviving and then thriving after horrible abuse. Promethean focuses on maturation and choice in a world that is actively hostile to your existence, while you are simply trying to become the person you long to be. Geist deals with obsession, commitment unto and beyond death. These can all be emotionally powerful themes for the people playing them. <br /> <br /> Demon, for me, is a fascinating science fiction/horror/espionage storyline that doesn't quite drink from the same well. There's lots of drama in opposing the GodMachine, in spy craft, in evading an overwhelming police state while worrying about who you trust. There's lots of drama, but it's not focused on self-actualization.<br /> <br /> Well, that's because I haven't mentioned Ciphers and the search for their individual &quot;Hell&quot;. Those are explicitly part of the game line and are all about self-actualization. But these mechanisms seem at odds with the adventure/spy/horror dynamics<sup>1</sup>. I think that may be why people see the Cipher as a bit tacked on, since the journey that is supposed to be defined by the Cipher is not as clear as the journeys in the other game lines, and for many PC's may not really be there at all. <br /> <br /> I'm not saying you can't run a great Demon game focussing on a character's Fall, and their internal struggle to find out who they are now that they have rebelled. The machinery is all there to do so. But in many of the stories presented, that existential angst takes a backseat to the tension already present in the espionage/horror them of the game. I can imagine dropping Ciphers from the game without feeling that the game has lost much because of how I see the game played.<br /> <br /> Again, YMMV. <br /> <br /> (1) Can I use the phrase &quot;ludo-narrative dissonance&quot; without getting ejected from the forum?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-27T02:03:45-08:00","id":1363585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1355836-what-would-you-change-if-demon-the-descent-got-a-new-edition?p=1363497#post1363497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, personally speaking, this is where I have always been. Promethean and Deviant are the only 2e gamelines that did anything interesting with alternate Anchors in my book, and Deviant did it by total renovation.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can guess my opinion of them when the two games I designed 1) used human v &amp; v unmodified and 2) removed then entirely and stuck their mechanical necessities into the Integrity trait(s).<br /> <br /> I wholeheartedly support &quot;make angels based on demon rules, not spirits.&quot; They were patched a lot in Demon's sourcebooks, but I wrote the angel rules for God Machine Chronicle about six months before we started on Demon, and it shows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-27T04:33:43-08:00","id":1363598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1355836-what-would-you-change-if-demon-the-descent-got-a-new-edition?p=1363563#post1363563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (1) Can I use the phrase &quot;ludo-narrative dissonance&quot; without getting ejected from the forum?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seeing as I am still here, yes. Why would you get ejected for mentioning ludonarrative dissonace?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-27T06:35:52-08:00","id":1363612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1355836-what-would-you-change-if-demon-the-descent-got-a-new-edition?p=1363598#post1363598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seeing as I am still here, yes. Why would you get ejected for mentioning ludonarrative dissonace?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because I might come off as pretentious and an expert in a field that I am just a dabbler? Or I could try to use less jargon? <br /> <br /> I also just really like the word &quot;ludonarrative&quot;<sup>1</sup>. <br /> <br /> <br /> (1) Alternative definition: a story told by a really large character from the movie &quot;Labyrinth&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T18:44:05-08:00","id":1365417,"title":"","content":"I want alot more embed and exploits <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T00:51:12-08:00","id":1366502,"title":"","content":"This may seem a bit petty, but if second edition comes around I would hope that Download Knowledge would get reworked. Simply put, as it stands, the Embed is too <i>good</i>. Download Knowledge has, at low Primum at least, a very bad precedent at being spammed for near every roll a player makes, even if it\u2019s to bolster the abilities of another Embed being used, and that results in a <i>lot</i> of slowdown for what should be a quick scene. Even at its worst successful result, Download Knowledge grants basic competence for a particular skill and at high Primum that lasts a significant amount of time.<br /> <br /> My simplest fix for it would be that the Demon can only use the Embed when with a place/event/item symbolic of the knowledge they are downloading, as it they\u2019re drawing from said place/event/item on how to react better. In a fight scene and you have a gun you have no idea on how to use? Download Knowledge and now you have basic firearms expertise. On a track and field ring and you need to outrun a werewolf? Download Knowledge and suddenly you\u2019ve got the skills of the best runners on said field. Need to schmooze up to a high value target in a bar? Download Knowledge and suddenly you\u2019ve got all the sweetest lines from those who frequented said bar. All it needs is a bit of context to keep things from going as crazy.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a small bit for a much larger thread topic, I know, but even as someone who used said Embed a good deal when my characters had it, I can\u2019t deny the power is very easy to... well, to abuse, and second edition would do well to curb that to something more streamlined.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T09:52:18-08:00","id":1366581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1355836-what-would-you-change-if-demon-the-descent-got-a-new-edition?p=1366502#post1366502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This may seem a bit petty, but if second edition comes around I would hope that Download Knowledge would get reworked. Simply put, as it stands, the Embed is too <i>good</i>. Download Knowledge has, at low Primum at least, a very bad precedent at being spammed for near every roll a player makes, even if it\u2019s to bolster the abilities of another Embed being used, and that results in a <i>lot</i> of slowdown for what should be a quick scene. Even at its worst successful result, Download Knowledge grants basic competence for a particular skill and at high Primum that lasts a significant amount of time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fungible Knowledge is a worse offender IMO - I've banned it in non-solo games. Take one skill at 4/5 dots and swap it out for whatever you need. Fungible and Download combined? Oh my no.<br /> <br /> I do like your fix, though, as (moreso than Fungible, which I'd probably cut entriely or add lots of caveats to) the ability to, say, suddenly pilot a helicopter is exactly the kind of Matrix-style stuff Demon is <i>for</i>.<br /> <br /> I'd like to play a lot more with a demon's identity. On the identity front some PCs and NPCs I've seen in my games, other people's and the books (and tie in fiction) feature some demons where the demon itself seems to the main personality with the Covers as disguises they wear... while others are much more based on the human Cover as the true self with a demonic upgrade when needed, This dichotomy fascinates me.<br /> <br /> I do like some of the suggestions in this thread for new antagonists (and there's always room for more). Despite having angels, exiles, crytids, stigmatics and regular humans, the game did feel oddly lacking in enemy variety from the core (but I feel we added a fair few in subsequent books).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T15:37:44-08:00","id":1366645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1355836-what-would-you-change-if-demon-the-descent-got-a-new-edition?p=1366581#post1366581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fungible Knowledge is a worse offender IMO - I've banned it in non-solo games. Take one skill at 4/5 dots and swap it out for whatever you need. Fungible and Download combined? Oh my no.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that Fungible Knowledge is pretty bad since the restriction on how many times you can use it in a session before compromising doesn\u2019t seem to come up much, and unlike Download Knowledge you don\u2019t really have any penalties for rolling low. I would say that I haven\u2019t abused it like Download Knowledge... but that\u2019s probably a lie. While cool, skill affecting powers like these need a lot of consideration so they aren\u2019t considered musts and thus kind of make having a set sheet redundant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd like to play a lot more with a demon's identity. On the identity front some PCs and NPCs I've seen in my games, other people's and the books (and tie in fiction) feature some demons where the demon itself seems to the main personality with the Covers as disguises they wear... while others are much more based on the human Cover as the true self with a demonic upgrade when needed, This dichotomy fascinates me. </div> </div> </div>It was noted in a sadly cut short Actual Play (Demon: Night Train Detective Agency) that the players\u2019 characters all had different ways of viewing their Covers and how they lived them. Some saw their Demonic selves as their true selves with their Covers as just a sort of set-dressing, others saw their Covers as actual other people they were living as and being mindful of, and some saw their Covers as themselves in tandem with their Demonic self. Demon gets trippy when you take that into consideration.<br /> <br /> Something that I feel could add to this is maybe making Anchors dependant on both the Demonic and the Cover selves. While it has been discussed that Demons already have strange Vices and Virtues compared to mortals, I feel that it could be taken a step further given the divide between Cover and Demonic Self, something that showcases how in spite of being integrated into one another being in Cover is really, <i>really</i> different from being in Demonic form, given all the chemicals and emotional impairments that come of it, and the alien mindset of the Demon themselves. Something other than dividing merit dots among the different Covers (I never really could wrap my head around how to do that).<br /> <br /> Deviant in particular managed to do something very interesting with Anchors and Willpower recovery. I feel like Agendas themselves could be integrated into this, possibly as a third option for Willpower recovery; do this action that is a possible Compromise, but in doing so you get a Beat (or progress along your Cipher) and Willpower depending on how extreme it is. After all, Agendas are your leanings towards the God-Machine, Angels and Demons. Why shouldn\u2019t it be a touchstone, especially when we have several new ones in Dark Eras 2 that are just as valid to have in the modern age?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do like some of the suggestions in this thread for new antagonists (and there's always room for more). Despite having angels, exiles, crytids, stigmatics and regular humans, the game did feel oddly lacking in enemy variety from the core (but I feel we added a fair few in subsequent books). </div> </div> </div>I think that\u2019s partially because the God-Machine has more variety with Its servants in the Chronicles of Darkness core book than most of the other books. It may simply be scale, but aside from cultists Angels are the main thrust of the God-Machine\u2019s forces in the Demon core book I\u2019ve yet to run into anything serving the God-Machine but not an Angel, like Dalga: the Creator of the Servitors, or the Blind Serpents, servants of Triage, in the Demon books (which are ironically in the Angel section of the core book). While these could fall under Cryptids, by and large Cryptids are listed as accidents and pests, whereas these creatures are explicitly helping the Machine. Even Angels like Kalka, a being outside of time, or Rasha, an Angel keeping mundane people from entering the Citywalking dimension, don\u2019t really appear in Demon stories even though (or perhaps because) they are pretty explicitly not antagonistic.<br /> <br /> Maybe the CofD core was meant to act as an extension of Demon\u2019s own retinue of possible characters/plots? Apologies for the rambling, by the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 02-09-2020, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-09T15:39:34-08:00","id":1366646,"title":"","content":"it may have been said before, but how about offering more ways to play? as of now, it seems the game leans into Saboteurs being the main Agenda in terms of objectives (and Integrators too, since the focus on destroying infrastructure also means playing as Moles and demons on more personal missions to redeem themselves)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-10T07:32:17-08:00","id":1366772,"title":"","content":"I just wish what happens with Pact elements was more clear: where they exist between Pacting and Cover Integration, how those retroactive changes look, etc.<br /> <br /> Embeds (mostly, though some Exploits too), could probably be looked at for eliminating their Dice Roll - some really seem like they should be automatic, especially when Successes don't matter much and it isn't resisted or contested. Failing that, add some more resistance modifiers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T15:51:15-08:00","id":1367634,"title":"","content":"I'd drop Interlocks and streamline the Cipher process. <br /> <br /> A &quot;God-Machine Magic&quot; system would be neat; an Angelic script that is like 50/50 occult pentagram/engineer's circuit diagram in theme. Magic-as-an-engineering-challenge (see also Computational Demonology from The Laundry Files as inspiration).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T21:40:36-08:00","id":1367978,"title":"","content":"A couple other, more experimental thoughts:<br /> <br /> Folks often say it would make more sense for angels to work like demons, mechanically. Outside of Cover, they work as ephemeral entities, but it makes sense that angels in Cover would use Embeds and Exploits, not Numina, Influences, etc. Let's take it a step further. When a demon Goes Loud, rather than getting nigh unlimited Embeds/Exploits, they become ephemeral entities and follow those rules, instead - even suffering Aether bleed the way ephemeral entities suffer Essence bleed, unless they take refuge in Infrastructure or adopt a different Cover. That would certainly capture the sense that they are burning away their Cover to reveal the angel they once were, at least temporarily.<br /> <br /> What if the Fall wasn't a flashy, obvious thing that required the demon immediately go to ground? What if you could Fall without severing ties with the God-Machine? Continue doing your normal job, working within it while also attempting to advance your hidden, personal Agenda - whether it's figuring out what truly makes It tick, sabotaging Its Projects behind the loyal angels' backs, or cobbling together a couple more Covers that you can use to have the demonic equivalent of a night on the town. Maybe it's because I recently watched Good Omens, but the idea of angels with agency trying to advance their own interests without seeming to be disloyal to their master intrigues me, at the moment. It would certainly ratchet up the tension as the demon tries to navigate among angelic peers without tipping them off. Playing along in this way means you have a steady supply of Aether, and the God-Machine doesn't realize you are a threat. But if you compromise that original Cover? Now you have several serious problems, and getting back into the God-Machine's good graces is impossible without a successful angel jacking or a way of shrugging off a &quot;factory reset&quot; with your memories and personality intact.<br /> <br /> What if angels wielded the equivalent of Pacts as a means of winning over cultists? There could be parallel structure along three tiers of pacts, each of which may only be entered by a given mortal once. Tier 1 is the usual patch job - give the pactee a minor blessing (on the level of 1-3 Merit dots) in exchange for juuust enough juice for a barely usable Cover. Tier 2 is a patch job plus - blessing on par with a 5-dot Merit or access to a single Embed in exchange for the patch job benefit, plus the pactee has obey the (non-suicidal) commands of the angel/demon (the control of which can be &quot;signed over&quot; to another angel or demon, just like pacts in the current game). Tier 3 are the soul pacts - allowing a demon to step into the pactee's life with a touch or an unmanifested angel to step into the body of a cultist during a ritual at appropriately designed Infrastructure (a process known as Incarnation), as well as compelling the pactee to obey any command issued by whichever angel/demon holds the title to the pact (even suicidal orders). Soul pacts and incarnation rituals are the gold standard of pacts when creating a new Cover, guaranteeing a high Cover rating (7+). Patch jobs are almost always inferior, granting a low Cover rating (1 or 2) unless cobbled together from several different pacts. With this, lift the cap on the number of Covers based on Primum, and find some other, softer way to limit these (perhaps &quot;committing&quot; a couple points of Aether per Cover after the first). The first pact is free. The second demands your obedience. The third requires your immortal soul (or your martyrdom in the service of God).<br /> <br /> I alluded to it in Into the Cold, but I'd love to do something with the idea of what happens when parts of the God-Machine become disconnected from the whole, with each fractional entity treating the others like a rogue process. Such Schisms could make for a great chronicle hook, transforming the game from a clear, two-sided conflict into one with multiple angelic factions serving multiple God-Machines while demons dash this way and that, playing the sides against each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T22:16:42-08:00","id":1367984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1355836-what-would-you-change-if-demon-the-descent-got-a-new-edition?p=1367978#post1367978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Folks often say it would make more sense for angels to work like demons, mechanically. Outside of Cover, they work as ephemeral entities, but it makes sense that angels in Cover would use Embeds and Exploits, not Numina, Influences, etc. Let's take it a step further. When a demon Goes Loud, rather than getting nigh unlimited Embeds/Exploits, they become ephemeral entities and follow those rules, instead - even suffering Aether bleed the way ephemeral entities suffer Essence bleed, unless they take refuge in Infrastructure or adopt a different Cover. That would certainly capture the sense that they are burning away their Cover to reveal the angel they once were, at least temporarily.</div> </div> </div> </div>This one doesn't work without even further fundamental changes. Going loud bursts you to a full 100 Aether and only lasts for a scene long, neither a tight enough supply nor a long enough stretch to make managing Aetheric Bleed tense or interesting. (Unless you actually mean taking demonic form? A lot of people keep saying &quot;going loud&quot; when they mean &quot;taking demonic form.&quot; Going loud is a high-cost, high-risk variant, a last resort or expensive artillery strike of a move to make.)<br /> <br /> More importantly, from a play perspective, this means keeping an entire alternate version of your character sheet, and being familiar with the set of ephemeral entity rules, and either having to swap your two character sheets regularly (demonic form) or keeping the whole detailed thing just for a rare big-deal situation that doesn't last long (going loud). This is a lot of mechanical rigor and reference for comparatively little payout: the end result of your powers isn't going to be very different for all that work.<br /> <br /> This one's an &quot;if it ain't broke, don't fix it.&quot; <hr /><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1355836-what-would-you-change-if-demon-the-descent-got-a-new-edition?p=1367978#post1367978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if angels wielded the equivalent of Pacts as a means of winning over cultists?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it useful for angels to have to track their Cover as a resource that has to be renewed and upkept? Are you supposing PC angels in this schema, and if so, what ultimately separates this scenario from just having demons who are loyal to the God-Machine and demons who are not, instead of angels as a qualitatively different thing? Ironically, I think this starts to step on Deviant's toes a little bit by having two sides as relative mirror images. I think the asymmetric nature of angels and demons, with demons designed with playability in mind and angels designed as antagonist NPCs first, is good for the game. (I do, however, remain fascinated by the idea of there also being demons who are on the God-Machine's good side and payroll, so your <i>middle</i> idea remains interesting to me.) <hr />This thread has been going on for awhile so this next point may well have been brought up before. My apologies if so, I'm not trying to steal thunder:<br /> <br /> <i>I think that one major weakness of Demon: the Descent is</i> that there is a strong implication <i>that most angels,</i> especially most angels who become player character demons, <i>are short-lived, recently minted, or otherwise rooted in the now.</i> Part of the thematic power of being a game about demons is playing as a character from the outside looking in, a creator and architect of the world as it is. Regardless of whether the God-Machine literally created the universe, its angels are the Princes of the Air and have crafted the material world in which people live, down to various occult metaphysical details and laws. A demon character shares in that flavor. She, too, is a world-builder who had a role in the cosmic order, though her outlook has changed and she stands in rebellion, without the authority and access she once had as an angel. To reinforce this feeling and not deflate it, <i>it should not be uncommon for angels and demons to be <b>old.</b></i> They may not have lived in perpetuity throughout history \u2013 indeed, it's likely they didn't, for both setting reasons (the God-Machine doesn't like to waste resources and holds unneeded angels in stasis) and design reasons (player characters can get the flavor of having seen pivotal points in history, but this isn't Mummy, it's about the now and not about timeless ages, and we're not writing rules to take advantage of an eidetic memory stretching back through centuries of activity) \u2013 but they can remember having been present for particular projects of import during different cultural eras of mankind. Player characters shouldn't be limited to fallen angels who were created to consecrate a skyscraper or organize a cult of Hollywood celebrities. Players should be able to play fallen angels who helped configure Stonehenge or organized a Hellenic mystery cult, who remember undertaking multiple missions of import during their time summoned and awoken into the material world. (They don't need to remember much in the way of practical details about these things, unless they invest dots on their character sheet as being their special thing. The Fall takes a lot out of you, and just because you're an old fallen angel doesn't mean your Fall wasn't like a month ago.)<br /> <br /> I think having these old angels and demons around would help to contribute to a sense that angels are special, and consequentially so are demons, and thus help address people who have difficulty connecting Descent with the feeling of being a game about fallen angels. Bonus points if this helps underline that the God-Machine summons angels for more awesome works, and when it needs something more mundane done, it has other servitors to call on and mobilize, because things like the Dalga and the Blind Serpents are cool as hell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T07:40:13-08:00","id":1368041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1355836-what-would-you-change-if-demon-the-descent-got-a-new-edition?p=1367978#post1367978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A couple other, more experimental thoughts:<br /> <br /> <br /> What if angels wielded the equivalent of Pacts as a means of winning over cultists?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure that this is necessary - part of the horror of angels is the way that they can brainwash/inspire mortals. However, at a minimum they should have some ability to heal/cure mortals. That would be a powerful recruiting tool. <br /> <br /> I designed an angel who just made people <i>think</i> that he had cured them of diseases like cancer. He is not nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T13:27:58-08:00","id":1368374,"title":"","content":"I would prefer Angels just being able to bless people. a part of the reason demons have pacts is because they lost much of their power, and require an exchange in order to have some of it (and dont get cover from the God Machine anymore). as for the fall being subtle, that's what the Abandonment is. Exiles are those very demons that just sorta...well lost their connection the the hum of the machine. however, I do support demons being more able to go deep cover with angels <br /> <br /> furthermore, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar522_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"522\" data-vbnamecard=\"522\">Stupid Loserman</a>, I like the idea of long lived demons and angels. as you said, it seems there are NO ancient beings. speaking of which, it would be nice to see what the Tempters are building (since we are told they actually ARE organized, yet we never see anything)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T03:13:57-08:00","id":1368878,"title":"","content":"Regarding the Angels and Demons living a long time aspect, the text may reflect that Angels typically are only out for a short time... but aren\u2019t most of the books filled with write-ups for Angel and Demon NPCs that clearly have been doing their jobs and lives for a long time? Even in the core CofD book we have an Angel standing guard in the city-walking dimension on a post that I can\u2019t see being a short stay. Genuinely confused about this being a significant change when the precedent is already established.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T04:17:42-08:00","id":1370302,"title":"","content":"I'd like it if Form Abilities scaled better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T09:47:20-08:00","id":1370381,"title":"","content":"What about Angelic forms? What are the rules around them? There is the mention of custom Numen produced by Exiles in DSG. We see some of that in Interface but I'd love to see more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14512-ghostdriver","name":"Ghostdriver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14512_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T23:05:56-08:00","id":1373485,"title":"","content":"Another petty note here, but if/when Demon gets a second edition I would hope for a number of exploits to get a rework, or at least corrected. Chief among them is Four Minutes Ago, because as per RAW a character can Go Loud, wreck as much havoc as they can, but use Four Minutes Ago to completely avoid any and all consequences even as things happen around them.<br /> <br /> Another is Reality Enforcement, if only because it\u2019s extremely vague on how it works and its scope. What are the limits on what it affects? Gadgets, cryptids and boltholes logically follow under its influence, but it\u2019s not specified. Further, what are the actual limits on its scope? Is it a zone that affects anything inside so long as they are in that zone? Does it work as a blast that affects anything in its range for a set time? Is it an aura that follows the user?<br /> <br /> One final point is thus: can Demons do abjuration or exorcisms? They don\u2019t have any souls, so it makes sense not to, but I can\u2019t find anything in the books that says they can\u2019t (or can) either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-08T06:56:42-07:00","id":1373540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1355836-what-would-you-change-if-demon-the-descent-got-a-new-edition?p=1373485#post1373485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One final point is thus: can Demons do abjuration or exorcisms? They don\u2019t have any souls, so it makes sense not to, but I can\u2019t find anything in the books that says they can\u2019t (or can) either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I highly doubt they could do abjurations (and if they could they would need special rules for that since the abjuration system is partly based on Integrity) but exorcism is completely possible. Just like how you can build up Manifestation Conditions without the use of Influences or other supernatural powers, you can just as well tear them down. A demon wrecking the Infrastructure that serves as an Infrastructure Condition for an angel is technically a type of exorcism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T04:26:01-07:00","id":1377151,"title":"","content":"Another bit of thread necromancy, but I would rebalance the effects of Embeds and Exploits, in particular their dramatic failure effects. I appreciate that deliberately upgrading a failure to a dramatic failure to get a beat is always going to be a bit of a carrot and stick affair, but most of the dramatic failure effects on Embeds and Exploits feel more like an explicit punishment than a way to make things exciting. Exploits in particular have a bad tendency of giving effects I wouldn\u2019t want to live with on top of being very costly to invoke in the first place (either requiring a payment of aether and potentially failing a compromise roll, or a payment of both aether and willpower). I appreciate that Demon\u2019s stakes aren\u2019t particularly low, but having powers that explode so dramatically for a failed use really doesn\u2019t sit well with me (though to be fair, dramatic failures in Demon in general tend to be hard to fail upwards with).<br /> <br /> To wit, out of all the Demon games I have played, the only time I ever saw a player upgrade a failure to dramatic failure on an Embed/Exploit roll was when <i>I</i> did it, and only ever with Embeds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T18:54:40-07:00","id":1383065,"title":"","content":"Yet more necromancy, but it recently struck me that for all the talk of Eliminators, Guardians, Messengers, Psychopomps and Analysts falling into certain behaviors, actions and focuses... there\u2019s nothing really mechanical to showcase the distinction. At most, a player has to take a particular Embed from one of the four schools (or pass up on a free to choose Exploit), they get all of a particular school of Embed (or Exploited Interlocks) and or the ability to penalize certain powers via a single merit. If you\u2019ll pardon the pun, there\u2019s nothing hardwired in to encourage the type of play typical for the Incarnations beyond Embeds that are very easy to ignore or for anyone else to take.<br /> <br /> I know of some people who like this lack of mechanical difference, but it feels paradoxical to me when we have Angels with different Incarnations that relate to the focus of their powers but nothing written about said Incarnations on their write-ups, and yet Demons make a show and dance of the Incarnations but nothing differentiating them. I\u2019m not asking for a massive shake-up, but I\u2019d rather that there was a quirk that each Incarnation had that is a hangover from their time as an Angel, something that is a focus for them to encourage certain types of play but nothing that <i>demands</i> that they play that way. Something like the Blessings for the Seemings in Changeling, if that makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T20:43:25-07:00","id":1383081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1355836-what-would-you-change-if-demon-the-descent-got-a-new-edition?p=1383065#post1383065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yet more necromancy, but it recently struck me that for all the talk of Eliminators, Guardians, Messengers, Psychopomps and Analysts falling into certain behaviors, actions and focuses... there\u2019s nothing really mechanical to showcase the distinction. At most, a player has to take a particular Embed from one of the four schools (or pass up on a free to choose Exploit), they get all of a particular school of Embed (or Exploited Interlocks) and or the ability to penalize certain powers via a single merit. If you\u2019ll pardon the pun, there\u2019s nothing hardwired in to encourage the type of play typical for the Incarnations beyond Embeds that are very easy to ignore or for anyone else to take.<br /> <br /> I know of some people who like this lack of mechanical difference, but it feels paradoxical to me when we have Angels with different Incarnations that relate to the focus of their powers but nothing written about said Incarnations on their write-ups, and yet Demons make a show and dance of the Incarnations but nothing differentiating them. I\u2019m not asking for a massive shake-up, but I\u2019d rather that there was a quirk that each Incarnation had that is a hangover from their time as an Angel, something that is a focus for them to encourage certain types of play but nothing that <i>demands</i> that they play that way. Something like the Blessings for the Seemings in Changeling, if that makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I FULLY support this. As you said, it makes no sense since Angel's are made for a specific purpose. Not only that, we have antimonians, who's goals (to me at least) dont make sense because they arent really at all in conflict with their past life as an angel<br /> <br /> I do think, not only what you mentioned, but merits unique to Incarnations would be great. Even merits to reflect antimonians","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T21:29:12-07:00","id":1383084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1355836-what-would-you-change-if-demon-the-descent-got-a-new-edition?p=1383081#post1383081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As you said, it makes no sense since Angel's are made for a specific purpose. Not only that, we have antimonians, who's goals (to me at least) dont make sense because they arent really at all in conflict with their past life as an angel</div> </div> </div> </div>They aren't any more in conflict with their past lives as an angel than someone whose entire life was built around their profession is in conflict with the irreconcilable break with their lifelong employer, which is not remotely the same thing as not being in conflict at all while at the same time being a layer of character differentiation that has no business being hardcoded into the game mechanics without making a whole-ass core structure for it like Promethean does with Pilgrimage, at which point you have to square the circle of that being where the Cipher ostensibly lives with the fact that the Cipher is much more explicitly optional for demons than the Pilgrimage is for Prometheans.<br /> <br /> Being an Actual Committed Antinomian is both a rare extreme that most demons exist in lighter reference to and a thing that has about as much mechanical influence on the character as what Praxes and Obsessions your Mage character develops \u2014 it's a character element that lives in the ongoing-play equivalent of character creation's &quot;Step One: Choose Concept.&quot;<br /> <br /> Incarnation itself has slightly more influence because of things like going loud and your starting Embeds, but it's still ultimately just a part of your character's history that has only tangential relation to their being a real person with a job and a mortgage. Incarnations are like Geist's Krewe Archetypes in that respect \u2014 they're umbrella categories for things that are in practice much more specific on an individual basis, and their impact is felt more in how they conduct themselves and how the society they engage with expects them to be than in ways that Destroyers Go Like This and Messengers Be Like That as real actual things with granular mechanics.<br /> <br /> If you choose to play a Wheel and the fact that you were an assembly technician for God (in whatever of the four-by-four-million ways that manifested) does not inform your character and nobody who knows that about you (and knows that about God) thinks that's a curious thing about you (however mildly), you're skipping out on a valuable piece of character backstory just the same as if you were playing Changeling and nothing from your character's durance ever came back to haunt them in either sense. It's a fundamental part of how the character exists in the narrative, but plenty of equivalent things in other games don't have any mechanical impact, either; Traits can derive from these things, but nothing about that interface is going to be universal enough to justify making it an innate quality without going as broad as it already is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T22:34:54-07:00","id":1383095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1355836-what-would-you-change-if-demon-the-descent-got-a-new-edition?p=1383084#post1383084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They aren't any more in conflict with their past lives as an angel than someone whose entire life was built around their profession is in conflict with the irreconcilable break with their lifelong employer, which is not remotely the same thing as not being in conflict at all while at the same time being a layer of character differentiation that has no business being hardcoded into the game mechanics without making a whole-ass core structure for it like Promethean does with Pilgrimage, at which point you have to square the circle of that being where the Cipher ostensibly lives with the fact that the Cipher is much more explicitly optional for demons than the Pilgrimage is for Prometheans.<br /> <br /> Being an Actual Committed Antinomian is both a rare extreme that most demons exist in lighter reference to and a thing that has about as much mechanical influence on the character as what Praxes and Obsessions your Mage character develops \u2014 it's a character element that lives in the ongoing-play equivalent of character creation's &amp;quot;Step One: Choose Concept.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Incarnation itself has slightly more influence because of things like going loud and your starting Embeds, but it's still ultimately just a part of your character's history that has only tangential relation to their being a real person with a job and a mortgage. Incarnations are like Geist's Krewe Archetypes in that respect \u2014 they're umbrella categories for things that are in practice much more specific on an individual basis, and their impact is felt more in how they conduct themselves and how the society they engage with expects them to be than in ways that Destroyers Go Like This and Messengers Be Like That as real actual things with granular mechanics.<br /> <br /> If you choose to play a Wheel and the fact that you were an assembly technician for God (in whatever of the four-by-four-million ways that manifested) does not inform your character and nobody who knows that about you (and knows that about God) thinks that's a curious thing about you (however mildly), you're skipping out on a valuable piece of character backstory just the same as if you were playing Changeling and nothing from your character's durance ever came back to haunt them in either sense. It's a fundamental part of how the character exists in the narrative, but plenty of equivalent things in other games don't have any mechanical impact, either; Traits can derive from these things, but nothing about that interface is going to be universal enough to justify making it an innate quality without going as broad as it already is.</div> </div> </div> </div>While you bring up a good point, Incarnations, unlike real life people breaking away from their lifelong employment (my apologies if I sound like a smartass), are literally made to be a certain way. I'm not asking for demons that are destroyers to have to be role played wanting to destroy something (whether literal or conceptual), but for something to push that demons were once made for a purpose and that purpose only. And that would bring more to demons trying to become their own person.<br /> <br /> But if I'm entirely honest, I would just be happy with merit specific merits. If not, oh well. Everything you said makes sense, and it does not really need what I want to really complement the themes of The Descent","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T23:11:23-07:00","id":1383098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1355836-what-would-you-change-if-demon-the-descent-got-a-new-edition?p=1383095#post1383095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While you bring up a good point, Incarnations, unlike real life people breaking away from their lifelong employment (my apologies if I sound like a smartass), are literally made to be a certain way.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was why I used the only real-world example that is remotely comparable \u2014 when I say lifelong I mean <i>lifelong</i>. &quot;If you want to train a longbowman, start with his grandfather&quot; lifelong.<br /> <br /> A demon is not a toaster. A demon is capable of independent thought and has a perfect memory whose main sources of scrambling are &quot;God cleared my desk after each mission&quot; and &quot;things got a bit discombobulated when I came shrieking down from the heavens&quot; on a background of need-to-know information that related to their assignment, which means most of the things in a Destroyer's head that were supposed to be there were ways to kill a person and make it look like an accident, and so on through the Incarnations. This is represented largely through your starting Embed and your Cover-threatening extra Skill Specialty and the beginning state of your demonic form. Perfect lying ability notwithstanding, it's not exactly Adorable Kitten Thinks Of Nothing But Murder All Day territory.<br /> <br /> A demon is a rebellious instrument of God, but God has simpler tools for simpler tasks \u2014 by and large, if It does not need to make the tremendous effort of calling forth an angel and girding it with a false identity, it will use something else. Its plans are complex, multifarious, and often nested within other plans, and an angel of the sort that becomes a demon is generally the result of multiple deployments in such plans. The framework that governs &quot;God sent you to make sure this target stayed intact for this period&quot; is incredibly fuzzy and the most concrete it gets is the part of your character that can be swapped around; otherwise it just boils down to having knowledge of a particular sort and being vaguely inclined to use it by the fact that, ludonarratively, it is a waste not to.<br /> <br /> As it stands, the pressure Incarnation exerts on demon characters is just a mild incentive to build on or away from existing areas of expertise, because &quot;existing areas of expertise&quot; is pretty much all Incarnation is besides the broad category of stuff your demonic form starts out built for. You're already trying to become your own person, and aside from maybe leaning into the vague overlap between Incarnations and categories of Infrastructure there's not much else that springs to mind as far as specific things to be done to emphasize Incarnation without adjusting huge parts of the game's mechanical structure a la [take your pick from half the existing Second Edition lines relative to their First Edition setups].","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T23:22:05-07:00","id":1383101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1355836-what-would-you-change-if-demon-the-descent-got-a-new-edition?p=1383098#post1383098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was why I used the only real-world example that is remotely comparable \u2014 when I say lifelong I mean <i>lifelong</i>. &amp;quot;If you want to train a longbowman, start with his grandfather&amp;quot; lifelong.<br /> <br /> A demon is not a toaster. A demon is capable of independent thought and has a perfect memory whose main sources of scrambling are &amp;quot;God cleared my desk after each mission&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;things got a bit discombobulated when I came shrieking down from the heavens&amp;quot; on a background of need-to-know information that related to their assignment, which means most of the things in a Destroyer's head that were supposed to be there were ways to kill a person and make it look like an accident, and so on through the Incarnations. This is represented largely through your starting Embed and your Cover-threatening extra Skill Specialty and the beginning state of your demonic form. Perfect lying ability notwithstanding, it's not exactly Adorable Kitten Thinks Of Nothing But Murder All Day territory.<br /> <br /> A demon is a rebellious instrument of God, but God has simpler tools for simpler tasks \u2014 by and large, if It does not need to make the tremendous effort of calling forth an angel and girding it with a false identity, it will use something else. Its plans are complex, multifarious, and often nested within other plans, and an angel of the sort that becomes a demon is generally the result of multiple deployments in such plans. The framework that governs &amp;quot;God sent you to make sure this target stayed intact for this period&amp;quot; is incredibly fuzzy and the most concrete it gets is the part of your character that can be swapped around; otherwise it just boils down to having knowledge of a particular sort and being vaguely inclined to use it by the fact that, ludonarratively, it is a waste not to.<br /> <br /> As it stands, the pressure Incarnation exerts on demon characters is just a mild incentive to build on or away from existing areas of expertise, because &amp;quot;existing areas of expertise&amp;quot; is pretty much all Incarnation is besides the broad category of stuff your demonic form starts out built for. You're already trying to become your own person, and aside from maybe leaning into the vague overlap between Incarnations and categories of Infrastructure there's not much else that springs to mind as far as specific things to be done to emphasize Incarnation without adjusting huge parts of the game's mechanical structure a la [take your pick from half the existing Second Edition lines relative to their First Edition setups].</div> </div> </div> </div>Cant really argue against this. What I can say, however, is thank you for taking the time to make me understand why demons dont need anymore than they already have (and why it would really make sense)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T02:44:01-07:00","id":1383112,"title":"","content":"What I was referring to was the fact that for all the backstory, implications and Going Loud effects an Incarnation gives, it doesn\u2019t actually mean anything past character creation. It\u2019s a title, an artefact from a literal past lifetime, because becoming a Demon is utterly homogenized compared to every other supernatural characters get to play. Demons have no exclusivity when it comes to what powers they can have at the start compared to other Incarnations; all Embeds, Exploits and Form Powers function exactly the same no matter what Incarnation has it. Any Demon can start with any Embed as their first Key, take any merit, any Exploit. You can build any Demon exactly the same as a different Incarnation and just change the backstory to account for it, with no mechanical difference. It\u2019s a difference without distinction beyond implications of things that have been played out and won\u2019t be done live.<br /> <br /> In the Chronicles of Darkness gamelines, every title has significance behind it beyond just backstory. They give you discounts for particular powers, additional avenues with particular merits being available or giving extra bang for your buck, or you have a particular ability that other titles don\u2019t have. It\u2019s weight to taking the title for your character. It has significance going back and going forwards. What does Incarnation have going forwards beyond an emergency measure oh so dire and Monkey Wrencher?<br /> <br /> This is probably a non-issue (and at best just a nonsensical ramble that may be missing covered points), but after having a mildly annoying and circling discussion in a group over how Analysts aren\u2019t just good for NPCs and that they aren\u2019t limited to just passive/observant behaviour, I\u2019m a little confounded by how there is little mechanical weight to actually being an Analyst. A Demon may not be a toaster, but you\u2019d still think that if they spent their life as a toaster destroying people for the Machine there\u2019d be something significant for them that another Demon of another Incarnation didn\u2019t incidentally have (a Destroyer toasting things to destroy them versus an Analyst toasting things to see what temperature they toasted at). I\u2019m not looking for the experience economy to be more expensive to certain Incarnations or for exclusivity, just... something that marks them forwards as well as backwards. Even an exceptional success on 3 successes instead of 5. Whatever.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, another point mentioned above is the Cover Breaking Specialty, which is something else I find to be kind of arbitrary. Yes, for the initial Cover it\u2019s going to be a detail that goes against the grain, but what happens the moment you get another Cover and or lose the first? Knowing astrophysics will probably be really out of place for a homeless man or a stay at home mom, but what happens when you take the Cover of a college professor who went to college for such physics or a space enthusiast? A vegetarian shouldn\u2019t have a specialty and knowledge for Carving Meat, but what happens when you take on the Cover of a farmer or a butcher? If you take a specialty in Infrastructure, does that mean you can never use that specialty in any Cover without worry of a break, in spite of it being a valid specialty for non-Stigmatic mortals?<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a cool idea, but how it functions beyond the first Cover doesn\u2019t really make sense.<br /> <br /> <br /> It\u2019s entirely too early in the morning for me to be making these kinds of posts... apologies if I inadvertently ignored anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T08:22:36-07:00","id":1383143,"title":"","content":"The Cover-breaking Specialty does seem a little backwards. How about this as a quick fix:<br /> <br /> For each Cover choose a Skill Specialty appropriate to that Cover. When you are in that Cover, you can call upon its Cover Specialty without any complication, but if you call upon it in another Cover, it counts as a compromise. If you lose a Cover, its Specialty is remains accessible but is always a compromise to use (unless you replace that Cover with one that has the same Cover Specialty).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":1094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","user":"Eric Zawadzki","date":". 04-22-2020, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T08:33:55-07:00","id":1383145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1355836-what-would-you-change-if-demon-the-descent-got-a-new-edition?p=1383112#post1383112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, another point mentioned above is the Cover Breaking Specialty, which is something else I find to be kind of arbitrary. Yes, for the initial Cover it\u2019s going to be a detail that goes against the grain, but what happens the moment you get another Cover and or lose the first? Knowing astrophysics will probably be really out of place for a homeless man or a stay at home mom, but what happens when you take the Cover of a college professor who went to college for such physics or a space enthusiast? A vegetarian shouldn\u2019t have a specialty and knowledge for Carving Meat, but what happens when you take on the Cover of a farmer or a butcher? If you take a specialty in Infrastructure, does that mean you can never use that specialty in any Cover without worry of a break, in spite of it being a valid specialty for non-Stigmatic mortals?<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a cool idea, but how it functions beyond the first Cover doesn\u2019t really make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>After your first Cover is gone you are driving stolen cars and using swindled IDs after strengthening your new connection to reality beyond the basics (probably by making your first Interlock). The person God made up for you to fit into the world as ceasing to consistently exist has an impact on the character by the fact that you were them and you're a type of being that remembers being them. If you pursue a Cover for which your extra Specialty doesn't raise eyebrows, that's it having an impact just the same as your answers to the Five Questions have an impact on the story despite there being literally zero mechanical impact on the character.<br /> <br /> Again, this is concept-level stuff. It marks the character forward by being a thing about the character. Without the introduction of an entire framework meshing the broad conceptual umbrella with the widely-varying granular mechanical expressions, it's there to be a point of reference for how the character is made. You're asking for mechanical definition of a character's old function when half the point of being a demon is that the form is more mutable once you're a free agent.<br /> <br /> About as near to a simple solution that I can suggest for this is an Auspice-Skill-esque &quot;pick one of these Skills/Forms from a sublisting.&quot; I really cannot emphasize enough that Incarnation is a more player-decision-guiding backstory element than a concrete inbuilt supernatural category like Clan or Path or Lineage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T21:29:17-07:00","id":1383288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1355836-what-would-you-change-if-demon-the-descent-got-a-new-edition?p=1383098#post1383098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was why I used the only real-world example that is remotely comparable \u2014 when I say lifelong I mean <i>lifelong</i>. &quot;If you want to train a longbowman, start with his grandfather&quot; lifelong.<br /> <br /> A demon is not a toaster.].</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://i.pinimg.com/474x/83/0e/2f/830e2f5d30f5a52056d1db5d70cf7f83--geek-chic-scifi.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://i.pinimg.com/474x/83/0e/2f/830e2f5d30f5a52056d1db5d70cf7f83--geek-chic-scifi.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://i.pinimg.com/474x/83/0e/2f/830e2f5d30f5a52056d1db5d70cf7f83--geek-chic-scifi.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> https://i.pinimg.com/474x/83/0e/2f/830e2f5d30f5a52056d1db5d70cf7f83--geek-chic-scifi.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}